# OSWP — Docker/WP-CLI Quick Reference

All commands assume you're issuing from the host
(`~/oswp` or `~/oswp/child`). Container name: `oswp-wordpress-1`.

## Syntax check a PHP file
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 php -l wp-content/themes/oswp-child/functions.php
```

## Pages

**List** (find an ID by slug):
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp post list --post_type=page --name=SLUG --allow-root
```

**Create:**
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp post create --post_type=page --post_title="Title" --post_name=slug --post_status=publish --allow-root
```

**Draft (hide from header nav without deleting):**
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp post update ID --post_status=draft --allow-root
```

**Delete:**
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp post delete ID --allow-root
```

## Menus

**List locations:**
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp menu location list --allow-root
```

**List items in footer menu:**
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp menu item list footer-menu --allow-root
```

**Add a page to footer menu:**
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp menu item add-post footer-menu POST_ID --allow-root
```

**Remove an item from footer menu** (needs the menu-item ID, not the
post ID — get it from `menu item list` above):
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp menu item delete MENU_ITEM_ID --allow-root
```

Note: header nav is automatic (lists all published pages) — nothing
to edit there directly; control visibility via page publish status.

## Images

**Regenerate all sizes for existing uploads** (needed after adding a
new `add_image_size()` — backfills old uploads that predate it):
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp media regenerate --allow-root
```

## Plugins / snippets (diagnostic)
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 wp plugin list --allow-root
```

## Reading files directly from the container
(useful when host/container content might have drifted — see
today's functions.php mix-up)
```bash
docker exec -i oswp-wordpress-1 cat wp-content/themes/oswp-child/functions.php
```

## Git (from ~/oswp/child unless noted)
```bash
git status
git add FILE
git commit -m "message"
git log --oneline -5
```

## Reminders from today
- Never `docker exec ... cat > file` to CREATE files — write with
  vim on the host instead. `docker exec` is for anything that must
  run *inside* WordPress (the `wp` commands above, `php -l`).
- Always pass `--allow-root` — this is a container.
- Hard-refresh (not just reload) when checking CSS/JS changes in
  browser — ordinary reload can serve cached assets.
